# Deep Analysis & Simplification Plan for TwinSec Demo & Presentation

## Problem Analysis

The mentor is currently confused by the application flow because:
1. **Overwhelming Surface Area & Component Density**: TwinSec has 20+ routes, floating widgets, tactical menus, and complex sidebars (Threat Profiles, DEF CON Briefs, S4 Talks, Case Files, Training Ledgers, Whitepapers, FAQs, etc.). A mentor looking at the app loses track of the core product story.
2. **Lack of a Guided 3-Step Flow**: The app currently does not guide an evaluator step-by-step through what TwinSec actually does (Explore Twin → Replay SCADA Incident → Generate SIEM Rules & PDF Report).
3. **Complex Simulation Interface**: In `/simulation`, there are multiple tabs (telemetry, packets, cve, sigma, cisa, ai_explain), sidebars, and terminals without clear callouts showing *what* to present first to the mentor.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Tomorrow's Presentation Strategy**: We will introduce a **"Mentor Guided Presentation Mode"** into the app. This adds a clean, 1-click step-by-step guided demo bar that walks the mentor through the exact 3-step story in 2 minutes:
> 1. **Step 1: Facility Twin Overview** (`/twin-engine` / `/facility/power`) — Show physics parameters & OT topology.
> 2. **Step 2: SCADA Incident & Hex Inspector** (`/simulation?sector=power`) — Demonstrate raw Modbus/S7 hex decoding, rotor speed drift, and interlock decisions.
> 3. **Step 3: Defense & Artifact Export** (`/simulation?sector=power`) — Export generated Sigma YAML detection rules, CEF logs, and PDF Dossier report.

> [!NOTE]
> All existing functionality remains 100% intact. Secondary pages (DEF CON talks, Whitepapers, etc.) are organized under a streamlined "Research Reference" section in the menu so they don't clutter the primary presentation.

